# =============================================================================
# Nightly-sweep Lychee ignore patterns (Tier 3 only)
# =============================================================================
# Identical to shared/config/.lycheeignore EXCEPT the mlsysbook.ai blanket
# exclusion is removed so the nightly crawl catches broken internal links.
#
# Why the split:
#   Tier 2 (validate-dev) runs BEFORE deploy — mlsysbook.ai content may not
#   yet be live, so checking those URLs produces false 404s. The blanket
#   exclusion in .lycheeignore is correct for pre-deploy CI.
#
#   Tier 3 (link-rot-nightly) runs nightly AFTER all subsites are deployed —
#   mlsysbook.ai IS live, so broken internal links are real 404s we need to
#   catch. This file removes that blanket exclusion so the nightly sweep
#   catches them.
#
# Usage: pass to infra-link-rot-nightly.yml via lycheeignore_path input.
# =============================================================================

# --- Localhost / private network ---
^https?://localhost(:\d+)?(/.*)?$
^https?://127\.0\.0\.1(:\d+)?(/.*)?$
^https?://192\.168\.\d+\.\d+(:\d+)?(/.*)?$
^https?://10\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+(:\d+)?(/.*)?$

# --- Slide decks behind Google auth (return 200 to logged-in users only) ---
^https://docs\.google\.com/presentation/

# --- Known transient 404s (re-add once content is restored) ---
^https://www\.reuters\.com/?$

# NOTE: mlsysbook.ai is intentionally NOT excluded here.
# The nightly sweep runs after deploy — broken mlsysbook.ai links are real 404s.

# --- Dev preview targets (not a concern for nightly) ---
^https://harvard-edge\.github\.io/cs249r_book_dev/

# --- SPA routes that use # for client-side routing (not document anchors) ---
^https://star-history\.com/#

# --- Unrendered JS template literals (false positives) ---
^https?://[^/]+/[^?#\s]*\$%7B[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\.[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*%7D

# --- GitHub avatar URLs ---
^https://github\.com/[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9-]*\.png(\?size=\d+)?$

# =============================================================================
# Anti-bot false positives — identical to .lycheeignore
